---
import Base from '@layouts/Base.astro';
import Hero from '@components/Hero.astro';
import { site, offers, contact } from '@config/site';
import '../styles/home-v10.css';
import '../styles/home-final.css';

const filmUrl = 'https://player.vimeo.com/external/443395616.sd.mp4?s=a7af94d210b59996f5308097b38adf0144d37a46&profile_id=139&oauth2_token_id=1223210874';
---
<Base title={site.name} description={site.description} path="/">
  <Hero />

  <main class="home-v10">
    <section class="film-v10" id="system-film" data-surface="dark" aria-labelledby="film-title">
      <div class="container-wide film-v10__grid">
        <div class="film-v10__copy">
          <span class="v10-kicker v10-kicker--light">SYSTEM FILM</span>
          <h2 id="film-title">Watch the evidence move from public source to decision.</h2>
          <p>The three-dimensional Evidence Axis appears once, in the hero. Here the workflow moves: public source, classification, traceable reasoning, then the decision output.</p>
          <div class="film-v10__chips mono"><span>PUBLIC SOURCE</span><span>CLASSIFY</span><span>TRACE</span><span>DECIDE</span></div>
        </div>

        <div class="film-v10__stage">
          <div class="film-v10__player">
            <video data-system-film muted loop playsinline autoplay controls preload="metadata" poster="/assets/v10/approved-visual-gallery.webp">
              <source src={filmUrl} type="video/mp4" />
            </video>
            <div class="film-v10__frame"><span>24-SECOND SYSTEM FILM</span><b>Evidence Axis / decision flow</b></div>
          </div>
          <figure class="film-v10__card film-v10__card--a"><img src="/assets/v10/corporate-strategy.webp" alt="Strategy team studying a global evidence map" /><figcaption>GLOBAL SIGNALS</figcaption></figure>
          <figure class="film-v10__card film-v10__card--b"><img src="/assets/v10/command-center.webp" alt="Business team studying strategic evidence" /><figcaption>DECISION ROOM</figcaption></figure>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="proofbar-v10" aria-label="Evidence Axis operating principles">
      <div class="container-wide proofbar-v10__grid">
        <article><span>01</span><b>100% traceable</b><p>Every material claim keeps a source.</p></article>
        <article><span>02</span><b>Source-backed</b><p>Public, identifiable, dated evidence.</p></article>
        <article><span>03</span><b>Decision-ready</b><p>Built around the move your team is considering.</p></article>
        <article><span>04</span><b>Audit-ready</b><p>The evidence trail stays visible.</p></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="gallery-v10" aria-labelledby="gallery-title">
      <div class="container-wide gallery-v10__grid">
        <div class="gallery-v10__copy">
          <span class="v10-kicker">RESEARCH IN CONTEXT</span>
          <h2 id="gallery-title">See the signals, the evidence and the decision in one system.</h2>
          <p>Strategy-room views, market signals, evidence matrices and decision interfaces are connected to the same research trail instead of living in separate decks.</p>
          <div class="gallery-v10__links"><a href="/method/">See how it works →</a><a href="/sample-report/">Open the sourced sample →</a></div>
        </div>
        <div class="gallery-v10__mosaic">
          <figure><img src="/assets/v10/command-center-approved.svg" alt="Decision-ready Evidence Axis interface" loading="eager" /></figure>
          <figure><img src="/assets/v10/corporate-strategy.webp" alt="Business professionals studying a global market map" loading="lazy" /></figure>
          <figure><img src="/assets/v10/global-signal.webp" alt="Global signal map control room" loading="lazy" /></figure>
          <figure><img src="/assets/v10/command-center.webp" alt="Strategic insights command center" loading="lazy" /></figure>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="insight-v10" aria-labelledby="insight-title">
      <div class="container-wide">
        <header class="v10-head v10-head--center"><span class="v10-kicker">WHY EVIDENCE AXIS IS DIFFERENT</span><h2 id="insight-title">Research that keeps proof separate from judgment.</h2><p>Fast summaries are easy. The hard part is preserving the source, evidence state, decision boundary and unresolved questions so confidence does not outrun the evidence.</p></header>
        <div class="insight-v10__grid">
          <article class="insight-card insight-card--cyan"><span>01</span><h3>Evidence before interpretation.</h3><p>Source, observation and fact stay attached before any strategic inference is written.</p><a href="/method/">See the method →</a></article>
          <article class="insight-card insight-card--blue"><span>02</span><h3>Source-backed and citable.</h3><p>Every material claim points to identifiable public evidence and a check date.</p><a href="/sample-report/">Open the sample →</a></article>
          <article class="insight-card insight-card--amber"><span>03</span><h3>Decision-scoped from the start.</h3><p>The question your team is deciding determines what gets investigated and what does not.</p><a href="/competitor-brief/">See the brief →</a></article>
          <article class="insight-card insight-card--violet"><span>04</span><h3>Judgment stays separated.</h3><p>Fact, Inference and Unknown never silently blur into one another.</p><a href="/method/">Trace the logic →</a></article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="offers-v10" id="services" aria-labelledby="offers-title">
      <div class="container-wide">
        <header class="offers-v10__head"><div><span class="v10-kicker">CHOOSE THE RIGHT BRIEF FOR YOUR DECISION</span><h2 id="offers-title">Start with the smallest brief that can settle the question.</h2></div><p>Broader research only makes sense when the decision genuinely needs a wider evidence field.</p></header>

        <div class="pricing-v10">
          <article class="price-card price-card--cyan">
            <div class="price-card__flag mono">FAST START</div>
            <span class="price-card__label mono">TWO-COMPETITOR</span>
            <h3>{offers.twoCompetitor.name}</h3>
            <p>{offers.twoCompetitor.scope} One defined decision question with a traceable evidence trail.</p>
            <div class="price-card__price"><small>STARTING PRICE</small><strong>{offers.twoCompetitor.priceDisplay}</strong><em>{offers.twoCompetitor.priceNote}</em></div>
            <div class="price-card__delivery"><small>DELIVERY</small><b>{offers.twoCompetitor.delivery}</b></div>
            <ul><li>Two named competitors</li><li>Evidence matrix + source register</li><li>Fact / Inference / Unknown separation</li><li>Decision implications</li></ul>
            <a href="/competitor-brief/">Start a Two-Competitor Brief →</a>
          </article>

          <article class="price-card price-card--orange">
            <div class="price-card__flag mono">BROADER READ</div>
            <span class="price-card__label mono">FIVE-COMPETITOR</span>
            <h3>{offers.fiveCompetitor.name}</h3>
            <p>{offers.fiveCompetitor.scope} Positioning, packaging and capability evidence surfaced together.</p>
            <div class="price-card__price"><small>STARTING PRICE</small><strong>{offers.fiveCompetitor.priceDisplay}</strong></div>
            <div class="price-card__delivery"><small>DELIVERY</small><b>{offers.fiveCompetitor.delivery}</b></div>
            <ul><li>Five named competitors</li><li>One research question</li><li>Contradictions surfaced</li><li>Decision implications</li></ul>
            <a href="/competitor-brief/">Start a Five-Competitor Brief →</a>
          </article>

          <article class="price-card price-card--violet">
            <div class="price-card__flag mono">STRATEGIC</div>
            <span class="price-card__label mono">STRATEGIC SCOPE</span>
            <h3>{offers.blueprint.name}</h3>
            <p>{offers.blueprint.scope} Deeper synthesis with a custom research boundary.</p>
            <div class="price-card__price"><small>PRICING</small><strong>{offers.blueprint.priceDisplay}</strong></div>
            <div class="price-card__delivery"><small>DELIVERY</small><b>{offers.blueprint.delivery}</b></div>
            <ul><li>Custom research boundary</li><li>Wider evidence base</li><li>Offer and category architecture</li><li>Strategic synthesis</li></ul>
            <a href="/strategic-blueprint/">Scope a Strategic Blueprint →</a>
          </article>

          <aside class="included-card">
            <span class="price-card__label mono">ALL BRIEFS INCLUDE</span>
            <div><b>Source-backed</b><p>Every material claim stays attached to evidence.</p></div>
            <div><b>Traceable</b><p>Walk a conclusion back to its source.</p></div>
            <div><b>Decision-ready</b><p>Built around a real commercial move.</p></div>
            <div><b>Unknowns visible</b><p>Missing evidence is named, not guessed.</p></div>
            <a href="/contact/">Need a custom scope? →</a>
          </aside>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="outputs-v10" aria-labelledby="outputs-title">
      <div class="container-wide">
        <header class="v10-head v10-head--center"><span class="v10-kicker">SAMPLE OUTPUTS THAT DRIVE DECISIONS</span><h2 id="outputs-title">Inspect the evidence. Inspect the reasoning. Then inspect the move.</h2><p>The homepage shows the working format directly: evidence matrix, decision brief, dashboard, workflow and strategy-room views.</p></header>
        <div class="outputs-v10__gallery outputs-v10__gallery--three">
          <figure class="v10-media"><img src="/assets/v10/evidence-matrix.svg" alt="Evidence Axis evidence matrix sample" loading="lazy" /><figcaption><span>EVIDENCE MATRIX</span><b>See what is supported and where certainty ends.</b></figcaption></figure>
          <figure class="v10-media"><img src="/assets/v10/decision-brief.svg" alt="Evidence Axis decision-ready output" loading="lazy" /><figcaption><span>DECISION OUTPUT</span><b>Traceable insight written for a real decision.</b></figcaption></figure>
          <figure class="v10-media"><img src="/assets/v10/decision-dashboard.webp" alt="Evidence Axis decision dashboard" loading="lazy" /><figcaption><span>DECISION DASHBOARD</span><b>Evidence, state and implication in one view.</b></figcaption></figure>
          <figure class="v10-media"><img src="/assets/v10/ai-comparison.svg" alt="Structured evidence compared with generic AI output" loading="lazy" /><figcaption><span>AI COMPARISON</span><b>Structure and traceability instead of fluent guesswork.</b></figcaption></figure>
          <figure class="v10-media"><img src="/assets/v10/approved-visual-gallery.webp" alt="Evidence Axis workflow interface" loading="lazy" /><figcaption><span>WORKFLOW</span><b>Public source → classify → trace → decide.</b></figcaption></figure>
          <figure class="v10-media"><img src="/assets/v10/decision-room.svg" alt="Business team reviewing strategic evidence" loading="lazy" /><figcaption><span>STRATEGY ROOM</span><b>Evidence becomes useful when it changes a move.</b></figcaption></figure>
        </div>
        <div class="outputs-v10__actions"><a class="v10-button v10-button--dark" href="/sample-report/">Open live sample report →</a><a class="v10-link" href="/method/">See the research method</a></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ai-v10" data-surface="dark" aria-labelledby="ai-title">
      <div class="container-wide ai-v10__grid">
        <div class="ai-v10__copy">
          <span class="v10-kicker v10-kicker--light">WHY A CHATBOT ALONE IS NOT THE PRODUCT</span>
          <h2 id="ai-title">Fluent answers are not the same as decision evidence.</h2>
          <p>General AI is useful for speed. Evidence Axis adds the parts a serious competitive decision still needs: a defined research boundary, identifiable public sources, visible evidence states and a traceable path from source to implication.</p>
          <ul class="ai-v10__points">
            <li>Claims stay attached to identifiable sources and check dates.</li>
            <li>Fact, Inference and Unknown remain visibly separate.</li>
            <li>The research question limits what is investigated and claimed.</li>
            <li>A decision implication can be traced backward to the evidence that produced it.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <figure class="ai-v10__visual"><img src="/assets/v10/ai-comparison.svg" alt="Comparison between generic AI output and structured, source-traceable Evidence Axis research" loading="lazy" /></figure>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="world-v10" data-surface="dark" aria-labelledby="world-title">
      <div class="container-wide world-v10__grid">
        <div class="world-v10__copy"><span class="v10-kicker v10-kicker--light">MARKET INTELLIGENCE</span><h2 id="world-title">See the world. Move with clarity.</h2><p>Competitive signals, public product evidence, market shifts and positioning moves are organized around the decision—not around a giant competitor encyclopedia.</p><a class="v10-button v10-button--light" href="/market-intelligence/">Explore Market Intelligence →</a></div>
        <figure class="world-v10__visual"><img src="/assets/v10/global-signal.webp" alt="Global market signal map" loading="lazy" /><div class="world-v10__metric world-v10__metric--one"><small>PUBLIC SIGNAL</small><b>Pricing change</b><span>source checked</span></div><div class="world-v10__metric world-v10__metric--two"><small>PRODUCT SIGNAL</small><b>Feature shipped</b><span>date confirmed</span></div><div class="world-v10__metric world-v10__metric--three"><small>OPEN QUESTION</small><b>Private adoption</b><span>unknown</span></div></figure>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="sample-v10" aria-labelledby="sample-title">
      <div class="container-wide sample-v10__grid">
        <figure class="v10-media v10-media--sample"><img src="/assets/v10/command-center.webp" alt="Business professionals reviewing strategic evidence" loading="lazy" /><figcaption><span>LIVE SAMPLE AVAILABLE</span><b>See the sourced report next</b></figcaption></figure>
        <div class="sample-v10__copy"><span class="v10-kicker v10-kicker--light">SEE THE STANDARD BEFORE YOU BUY</span><h2 id="sample-title">Intercom × Zendesk. Eight first-party sources. Visible evidence states.</h2><p>The live sample shows the research standard, source register, Fact / Inference / Unknown separation and the limits of what public evidence can establish.</p><div><a class="v10-button v10-button--light" href="/sample-report/">View Sample Report →</a><a class="v10-link v10-link--light" href="/report/evidence-axis-sample-intercom-vs-zendesk.pdf">Open PDF</a></div></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="final-v10" aria-labelledby="final-title"><div class="container-wide final-v10__panel"><div><span class="v10-kicker">START SMALL</span><h2 id="final-title">Make the next competitive decision with evidence attached.</h2><p>Send the competitors, the question and the context that changes what “better” means for your team.</p><div class="final-v10__actions"><a href="/contact/">Start a Brief →</a>{contact.email && <a href={`mailto:${contact.email}`}>{contact.email}</a>}</div></div><img src="/assets/v10/corporate-strategy.webp" alt="Business professionals reviewing evidence in a market intelligence room" loading="lazy" /></div></section>
  </main>
</Base>

<script>
  const film = document.querySelector('[data-system-film]');
  if (film instanceof HTMLVideoElement) {
    let onScreen = true;
    const sync = () => { if (document.hidden || !onScreen) film.pause(); else film.play().catch(() => {}); };
    const io = new IntersectionObserver(([entry]) => { onScreen = Boolean(entry?.isIntersecting); sync(); }, { threshold: .08 });
    io.observe(film);
    film.addEventListener('timeupdate', () => { if (film.currentTime >= 24) film.currentTime = 0; });
    document.addEventListener('visibilitychange', sync);
  }
</script>
